WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.687
This final slide provides official NumPy learning resources and examples of how NumPy appears in current data roles.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:17.907
The official beginner guide is especially useful when you need to review array creation, indexing, shape, broadcasting,

00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:19.722
and common calculations.

00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:24.460
The best way to continue is to practice on small numerical problems.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:30.225
Take a Python list from an earlier module and convert it to a NumPy array.

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:35.125
Then try to replace a manual loop with a vectorized calculation.

00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:44.250
In the next module, we move into Pandas, where the same array-oriented ideas become part of a more complete workflow for

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.462
cleaning, transforming, summarizing, and combining tabular data.
